A standalone Rust CLI with local system status, shell completions, and an embedded operational guide.

## Installation

This generated project has no published artifacts yet. Once its owner publishes a release, download the archive for your operating system from [GitHub Releases]({{ repository }}/releases), extract it, and place `{{ binary }}` on your PATH. The release workflow prepares drafts for owner review.

## Usage

```console
{{ binary }} system status
{{ binary }} --help
{{ binary }} completion bash
AGENT=1 {{ binary }} skill
```

`system status` prints readiness, package version, and the current directory. Human output uses labeled status lines; `AGENT=1` emits compact key-value lines. Home directories appear as `~` in display output.

`--version` prints only the version and newline. Every command accepts `--help` and `-h`. Root invocation and `system` without a verb print help.

Read the complete [operational skill](skills/{{ binary }}/SKILL.md), also embedded verbatim in `{{ binary }} skill`. Contributor commands and repository constraints live in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).

